        "id": 14267,
        "name": "Pulseglazer",
        "username": "Pulseglazer",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/f04885/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-29T00:30:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<div>So, the new cards plus the ARG plus proctoring leaving me super bored plus an abundance of post its... I decided to try and categorize the heroes. &nbsp;Many can fit into multiple categories, but I think these more or less fit:</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\n<strong>Swiss Army Knife: </strong>This category of character can do a bit of everything. They kill ongoings, do lowish steady damage, and just generally fill needs on the team. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The characters: Omnitron X, Tempest, Wraith (all versions), Fanatic, Dark Watch NightMist, Tachyon</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\n<strong>Superior Support:</strong> &nbsp;These guys don’t damage much, but they make the game easier by making other hero’s jobs easier. &nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Characters: Visionary (both), Parse, Captain Cosmic, Team Leader Tachyon, Argent Adept (normal and Prime Wardens), Bunker (Engine of War and GI)</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\n<strong>Solo Tier: </strong>&nbsp;These are guys with a bit longer set up who do a lot to support a team, like the Swiss Army Knife class, but they tend to have a semi-ultimate set up where if they’re the last hero, the game is still very often in your hands. &nbsp;These guys can support, but also benefit a ton from any extra support. &nbsp;This is my favorite group.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Characters: Nightmist, Scholar, Legacy (any), Nightmist, Hunted Naturalist, Sky Skraper.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\n<strong>Glass Cannons: </strong>&nbsp;Fairly self-explanatory. &nbsp;These guys deal damage and lots of it, early and often. &nbsp;There are some of these that just crush face.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Characters: Chrono Ranger, Knyfe, DW Fixer, Expatriette (Both), Sentinels, Absolute Zero (Termination and F6), Prime Wardens Tempest, Golem Unity, Ra</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\n<strong>Long Term Reward:</strong> &nbsp;These are your builders. &nbsp;They tend to look for power combos. They can work otherwise, but they’re really about a giant attack down the line while they do whatever else early.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The Characters: Absolute Zero, Eternal Haka, Redeemer Fanatic, Super Scientific Tachyon, Bunker, Termi-Nation Unity, Horus Ra</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>\n<strong>Combo:</strong> &nbsp;These are similar to long term reward, except they don’t want a super combo or uber set up, but they need a few different combos that they can set up for themselves and others.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Characters: Mr. Fixer, Kvothe, Setback, Guise (and Santa Guise) Prime Wardens Fanatic, Prime Wardens Haka, Scholar of the Infinite, Unity, Prime Wardens Captain Cosmic, Chrono Ranger Best of Times, Rogue Agent Knyfe, Admant Sentinels, Naturalist</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>So, I know people can fit more than one place, but, in general, agree or disagree with the categories and placement? Other thoughts?</div><div>&nbsp;</div>",
